    "title": "Free Trial - Netflix Guide - IGN",
    "text": "Focus ResetTask Search Checklists Guides Markers VideosSort and FilterNo ResultsChecklists New ChecklistAll ListsMy ChecklistsAllAll ListsMy ChecklistsHow creative can you get with your first free checklist?Create a free accountFree TrialBy Jon Ryan, Blythe Dujardin, Jacob Kienlen, +2.0k morePosted: Mar 20, 2026 8:54pm UTCNetflix does not offer any type of free trial. Even though the service does have a free trial page in the Netflix help center, it simply states that Netflix does not offer free trials and points to links on how to change your Netflix plan or cancel your membership. Netflix also does not offer any streaming bundles or discounts, so the only way to access Netflix 'for free' is through phone and internet providers, most notably through Xfinity's Streamsaver plan and as a perk on select Verizon plans. While the number of streaming services that do offer free trials continues to dwindle, some standouts include Hulu (30-day free trial), Prime Video (30-day free trial), and Apple TV (7-day free trial). Up Next: Netflix Original SeriesPreviousPlans and PricingNextNetflix Original SeriesTop Guide SectionsPlans and PricingFree TrialNetflix Original SeriesWas this guide helpful?Leave feedbackIn This GuideNetflixNetflixLearn moreGo to comments",
